# A list is typed through the bottom instance of nil's type and a
# choice-typed contract of cons. This module holds the bottom instance; the
# contract of cons is cons_filtered_choice of choice_polymorphism.
#
# A constant whose type parameter only its use site fixes, nil, gets one
# ground contract at the bottom instance of its type, list_type top, where top is
# the library's top, the term that stands for no answer. A use site then needs no instance of nil's parameter,
# only an upper bound: list_type top is below every list_type A by
# monotonicity. The other lemma is the applied form of a point-free contract
# already in the library, successor_filtered of parallel_types, so that it
# matches terms written by application.
#
# Every lemma here is a theorem of λ-lattice-unit-η (CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Terms"); each declaration cites its paper proof. None uses induction. This module declares no define: it uses filter_by and
# list_type (parallel_lists), filter_nat (parallel_types), successor and nil
# (prelude), with which it is compiled.

# The bottom instance of nil's type: nil is a list of elements of the empty
# choice. Used from right to left, it adds the filter to the class of nil,
# which is also the class of zero, true and konstant (one term).
